description.narrative:
Since 2013 and until end of the project in December 2020, the specific results achieved could be described as follows:
State level:
- 218 budget programs analysed from gender perspective in all sectors at state (100 programs) and local (118 programs) level, and are currently being improved to be more responsive to the needs of women and men/closing gender gaps;
- 1,075 budget passports at local level have gender aspects included in 2020;
- around 40 budget passports at state level have gender aspects included in 2020;
- around 3,000 public officials at state and local level had a training in GRB;
Local level:
- All oblasts (municipalities in Ukraine, which are 24 in total) were working on GRB on continuous analysis and change in programs to make them more responsive to women and men in Ukraine
- Amalgamated territorial units (hromadas) started to work with GRB  through direct assistance or cooperation with U-Lead, UN Women, NDI;
- 40% hromadas created as of 1 January 2020 had training in GRB (training in 2021 was limited due to Covid-19 reasons);
GRB institutionalization in legislative and strategic documents, results are as follows:
-Strategy for PFM Reform in Ukraine (2017-2020) and draft PFM reform Strategy 2021-2025 include gender considerations as part of program budgeting at both state and local levels;
- Methodological Recommendations for GRB for key spending units (KSUs) were adopted by an Order of the Ministry of Finance in January 2019, that will provide recommendations to all ministries in Ukraine to do gender analysis of budget programs.
